Plan: Free Account Limits + Premium Feature Gating
Context
The app has a partially-implemented premium system (PremiumContext from sprint 18) that reads is_premium from Supabase but lacks feature-gating utilities and proper UI feedback. This sprint completes that foundation and exposes the first real free-tier limits:

Daily swipe limit (20/day) — already tracked in AsyncStorage, but the "limit reached" state only shows a plain text overlay. Needs a proper upgrade prompt.
Advanced filter locks — Gender and Age filters are already wrapped in PremiumLockWrapper, but it calls Alert.alert() instead of showing a rich upgrade modal.
PremiumContext — needs canUseFeature() for clean per-feature checks.
New components — UpgradeModal (full benefits + CTA) and PremiumBadge (inline label).
Email validation — frontend format check + backend DNS domain validation before storing temp registration.
Files to Create
File	Purpose
src/components/UpgradeModal.tsx	Full-screen upgrade modal with benefits list and CTA
src/components/UpgradeModal.styles.ts	Styles for UpgradeModal
src/components/PremiumBadge.tsx	Small inline badge labelling premium features
src/screens/PremiumScreen.tsx	Placeholder screen navigated to from "Obtener Premium"
Files to Modify
File	What changes
src/context/PremiumContext.tsx	Add Feature type + canUseFeature(f) function
src/components/PremiumLockWrapper.tsx	Replace Alert with local UpgradeModal state
src/screens/SwipeScreen.tsx	Upgrade the limitOverlay to show UpgradeModal
src/navigation/AppNavigator.tsx	Register PremiumScreen in the authenticated stack
src/screens/register/Phase1Email.tsx	Add email format regex validation in handleNext
supabase/functions/auth-register-phase1/index.ts	Add DNS domain existence check via DNS-over-HTTPS
Implementation Details
1. PremiumContext — Feature Gating
Add a Feature union type and a canUseFeature helper. Export the type so consumers can use it safely.

export type Feature = 'unlimited_swipes' | 'gender_filter' | 'age_filter';

const PREMIUM_FEATURES: Record<Feature, boolean> = {
  unlimited_swipes: true,
  gender_filter: true,
  age_filter: true,
};

// Add to context value:
canUseFeature: (feature: Feature) => isPremium || !PREMIUM_FEATURES[feature]
Context interface becomes:

interface PremiumContextValue {
  isPremium: boolean;
  loading: boolean;
  refetch: () => void;
  canUseFeature: (feature: Feature) => boolean;
}
2. UpgradeModal Component
Modal with transparent + animationType="fade"
Backdrop: BlurView blurType="light" blurAmount={20} + dark overlay rgba(0,0,0,0.45)
Card: white glass card (rgba(255,255,255,0.92)) with borderRadius: 24, shadow
Content:
Crown icon (Ionicons "star" in purple)
Title: "Hazte Premium"
Subtitle: "Desbloquea todas las funciones"
Benefits list (with checkmark icons):
Swipes ilimitados cada día
Filtros avanzados (género, edad)
Ver compatibilidad detallada
Soporte prioritario
Primary CTA: purple button "Obtener Premium" → navigates to 'Premium' screen and closes modal
Secondary link: "Ahora no" (grey text, closes modal)
Props: visible: boolean, onClose: () => void
3. PremiumBadge Component
Small inline pill badge, no state or context dependency. Pure presentational.

interface Props {
  size?: 'sm' | 'md';
}
sm: paddingHorizontal 6, paddingVertical 2, fontSize 10, lock icon size 9
md (default): paddingHorizontal 10, paddingVertical 4, fontSize 12, lock icon size 11
Background: rgba(124,58,237,0.12), border rgba(124,58,237,0.25), text/icon #7C3AED
Text: "Premium", icon: Ionicons "lock-closed"
4. PremiumLockWrapper — Use UpgradeModal
Replace the Alert.alert() fallback with local modal state:

const [modalVisible, setModalVisible] = useState(false);

const handleUpgrade = () => {
  if (onUpgradePress) {
    onUpgradePress();
  } else {
    setModalVisible(true);
  }
};

// Add at end of return:
<UpgradeModal visible={modalVisible} onClose={() => setModalVisible(false)} />
5. SwipeScreen — Improved Limit Overlay
Replace the current plain limitOverlay with a richer layout. Add local upgradeModalVisible state.

Replace:

{!canSwipe && currentProfile && (
  <View style={styles.limitOverlay}>
    <Text style={styles.limitText}>Limite diario alcanzado</Text>
  </View>
)}
With:

{!canSwipe && currentProfile && (
  <View style={styles.limitOverlay}>
    <BlurView blurType="light" blurAmount={18} style={StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject} />
    <View style={styles.limitContent}>
      <Ionicons name="flash-off" size={32} color="#7C3AED" />
      <Text style={styles.limitTitle}>Límite diario alcanzado</Text>
      <Text style={styles.limitSubtitle}>
        Has usado tus {SWIPE_LIMIT} swipes de hoy.{'\n'}Vuelve mañana o hazte Premium.
      </Text>
      <TouchableOpacity style={styles.limitUpgradeBtn}
        onPress={() => setUpgradeModalVisible(true)}>
        <Text style={styles.limitUpgradeBtnText}>Obtener Premium</Text>
      </TouchableOpacity>
    </View>
    <UpgradeModal visible={upgradeModalVisible}
      onClose={() => setUpgradeModalVisible(false)} />
  </View>
)}
Also add upgradeModalVisible to the styles file for the new limitContent, limitTitle, limitSubtitle, limitUpgradeBtn styles.

6. PremiumScreen Placeholder
Simple screen with:

Glass header with back button
Purple gradient hero area with crown icon + "Próximamente"
Text: "Estamos trabajando para traerte la mejor experiencia Premium."
Back navigation via navigation.goBack()
Register in AppNavigator.tsx:

<Stack.Screen name="Premium" component={PremiumScreen} />
7. Phase1Email — Frontend Format Validation
In handleNext(), after the empty checks, add before calling onNext:

const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
if (!emailRegex.test(email.trim())) {
  Alert.alert('Error', 'El formato del email no es válido');
  return;
}
Remove the verbose console.log calls while touching the file (the garbled emoji logs suggest encoding issues in the file — leave them as-is to minimise diff; only add the validation).

8. Backend DNS Domain Check
In supabase/functions/auth-register-phase1/index.ts, after the email format regex check, add domain existence validation using Google's DNS-over-HTTPS API:

const domain = body.email.split('@')[1];
try {
  const dnsRes = await fetch(
    `https://dns.google/resolve?name=${encodeURIComponent(domain)}&type=MX`,
    { headers: { Accept: 'application/dns-json' } }
  );
  const dnsData = await dnsRes.json();
  if (dnsData.Status === 3) {
    // NXDOMAIN — domain does not exist
    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({ error: 'El dominio del email no existe' }),
      { status: 400, headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } }
    );
  }
  // If NOERROR but no MX records, accept anyway (some domains use A for mail)
} catch {
  // DNS check timed out or failed — allow through to avoid blocking valid users
}
Only a definitive NXDOMAIN (Status === 3) should block registration. Network errors are silently ignored.

Verification
Swipe limit UI — in SwipeScreen, deplete swipes manually (or set swipesUsed = SWIPE_LIMIT) and confirm the new overlay shows with UpgradeModal accessible.
Filter locks — open FiltersScreen as a free user, tap Gender or Age filter, confirm UpgradeModal appears (not an Alert).
PremiumBadge — visually verify it appears where used.
PremiumScreen — tap "Obtener Premium" in any upgrade modal, confirm navigation to placeholder screen with back button working.
Email validation — enter notanemail in Phase1, confirm frontend error. Enter user@nonexistentdomain12345.xyz and submit, confirm Edge Function returns 400.
canUseFeature — add a console.log or test call to confirm canUseFeature('unlimited_swipes') returns false for free users and true for premium users.
